-- title:
--   Adjoining -1 halves the index of Γ₁(N), N≥ 3
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a natural number, assumed nonzero, and suppose $3 \le N$. Inside $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ consider the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_1(N)$, consisting of the matrices whose reduction modulo $N$ has diagonal entries $1$ and lower-left entry $0$, and the cyclic subgroup $\langle -1\rangle$ generated by $-1$, i.e. the subgroup of integer powers of $-I$. The theorem asserts the equality of natural numbers
--   $$2 \cdot [\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}) : \Gamma_1(N) \vee \langle -1\rangle] \;=\; [\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}) : \Gamma_1(N)],$$
--   where $\Gamma_1(N) \vee \langle -1\rangle$ is the subgroup generated by $\Gamma_1(N)$ and $-1$ (equal, since $-1$ is central, to $\pm\Gamma_1(N)$), and both indices are the subgroup indices in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ in the sense of Mathlib's `Subgroup.index`. Thus the index of $\Gamma_1(N)$ is exactly twice that of $\pm\Gamma_1(N)$; the hypothesis $3 \le N$ is what guarantees $-1 \notin \Gamma_1(N)$, the conclusion failing for $N = 1, 2$.
--
--   This is the standard bookkeeping fact that for $N \ge 3$ the group $\Gamma_1(N)$ does not contain $-I$ and therefore has index $2$ in $\pm\Gamma_1(N)$, the group acting faithfully on the upper half-plane. It is used to convert between indices of $\Gamma_1(N)$ and of $\pm\Gamma_1(N)$ in the degree and genus computations for the modular curves $X_1(N)$, and is cited in the determination of the index and double-coset count for $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ and in the relative degree computation for the function field of $X_1$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CongruenceSubgroup_two_mul_index_gamma1_sup_zpowers_neg_one.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open scoped MatrixGroups

theorem CongruenceSubgroup.two_mul_index_gamma1_sup_zpowers_neg_one
    (N : ℕ) [NeZero N] (hN : 3 ≤ N) :
    2 * (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma1 N ⊔ Subgroup.zpowers (-1 : SL(2, ℤ))).index = (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma1 N).index := by sorry
